@page "/lov/ukazka"
@*
    EXAMPLE TASK PAGE – copy this file to start a new task:
      1. Copy it within this folder (Components/Pages/Tasks) and rename it, e.g. Leden.razor.
      2. Change @page to the task's address, e.g. "/lov/leden". Players see the address once the task is
         active, so keep it neutral (no hints in it).
      3. Rebuild, then in Administrace → Úkoly edit the task and pick that address under "Stránka úkolu".

    TaskShell does the rest: the title (= task name), the "back to the hunt" link and access. Players only get
    in once the task is active; before that they see "not found". Admins can always preview.
    Inside, "task" is the TaskContext: task.HuntTask (name, ...), task.IsCompleted, and
    task.CompleteAsync() to call when the player solves it (gives them the checkmark on /lov).
*@

<TaskShell Context="task">
    <p>Tady bude zadání úkolu <strong>@task.HuntTask?.Name</strong>.</p>

    @if (task.IsCompleted)
    {
        <p><strong>Splněno!</strong> Na stránce Lov už u tohoto úkolu máš fajfku.</p>
    }
    else
    {
        <MudButton Variant="Variant.Filled" Color="Color.Primary" OnClick="task.CompleteAsync">Splnit (ukázka)</MudButton>
    }
</TaskShell>
